  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tutorial_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4d7c9e7db44e66f4aa84fe9d686bf156, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 230618705920
    m_Localized: Welcome to the ChessEscape Tutorial.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 237124071424
    m_Localized: ChessEscape unfolds across 204 levels, in which the traditional
      chessboard becomes the stage where you will challenge your intelligence.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 240546623488
    m_Localized: Your goal is to guide the King to the top-right square, where the
      door is located. This square corresponds to H8 on a traditional chessboard.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1643788775424
    m_Localized: The King always starts on the bottom-left square, equivalent to
      A1 on a traditional chessboard.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1674725961728
    m_Localized: By default, the King has 3 Movement Points (MP) each turn
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1708913733632
    m_Localized: Whenever you select him, his movement range will appear highlighted
      in green.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1739418906624
    m_Localized: The same will happen if you choose the Pawn or another Allied Piece
      such as the Knight, Bishop, Rook, or Queen.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 4847662411776
    m_Localized: The movement range display can be turned off by tapping the same
      piece again.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 4782298378240
    m_Localized: "When you press the \u201CStart\u201D button, the King will be selected
      by default."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5022481002496
    m_Localized: The King and Allied Pieces can eliminate Enemy Pieces if they are
      within their attack range. A fuchsia square will light up when this option
      is available.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5100088209408
    m_Localized: For Enemy Pieces, tapping on them will reveal their Lethal Attack
      Range and Ranged Attack Range. Tap again to hide their range.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5127837724672
    m_Localized: By default, the King has 5 Action Points (AP) each turn. These are
      needed for the King to command Allied Pieces to move.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5158242234368
    m_Localized: Each turn lasts 30 seconds. If you obtain a Golden Clock, you gain
      15 extra seconds for that turn.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5188302811136
    m_Localized: The King has 7 Lives (turns), which can be increased or decreased
      with items.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5223002288128
    m_Localized: You will also find items that grant extra AP and MP to the King,
      or increase the movement range of Allied Pieces.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5251418697728
    m_Localized: 'More information about items and pieces can be found in the ChessEscape
      Codex. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5284742443008
    m_Localized: The notification interface will inform you whenever you obtain a
      new page.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5317822918656
    m_Localized: "That\u2019s it! Now you can begin the adventure of guiding the
      King to the Final Room.\nYou can do it!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 262470894759936
    m_Localized: When Enemy Pieces attack from a distance, they reduce MP from the
      King or AP if it is an Allied Piece. You will notice it by the threat line
      projected by the Enemy Piece.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 397500686151680
    m_Localized: This is the visual summary of the objects that shape the universe
      of ChessEscape.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
